# UI Rules

## Product Feel

Vrompt should feel like a modern developer tool.

Avoid making the product look like a generic AI chatbot.

The interface should emphasize:

- structure
- clarity
- progress
- project context
- reviewability
- generated artifacts

## Guided Interview

The interview should feel progressive rather than like a giant form.

Prefer:

- focused questions
- clear sections
- visible progress
- sensible defaults
- editable answers

## Review

Generated project context should be reviewable before export.

Users should understand:

- what was generated
- what changed
- what target tool will receive
- where limitations exist

## Components

Prefer small reusable components with clear responsibilities.

Avoid giant page components containing all business logic.

Business logic should live outside presentation components when practical.

## Accessibility

Use semantic HTML.

Support:

- keyboard navigation
- visible focus states
- readable contrast
- useful labels
- meaningful error messages

## Responsive Design

The primary workflow must work on common desktop and laptop sizes.

Do not optimize solely for a single viewport.

## Animation

Use motion selectively.

Animation should communicate:

- progress
- state changes
- hierarchy

Do not animate every element merely because the framework can do it.
